01:55:14.590 --> 01:55:14.950
I'm sure.

01:55:14.950 --> 01:55:15.540
I'm sure.

01:55:15.540 --> 01:55:18.520
In fact, I guarantee you he
has that number in his brain.

01:55:18.520 --> 01:55:20.230
I haven't talked
to him in 15 years,

01:55:20.230 --> 01:55:22.240
but I guarantee you that
number is in his brain,

01:55:22.240 --> 01:55:23.840
and he's probably
training for it.

01:55:23.840 --> 01:55:24.965
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I love it.

01:55:24.965 --> 01:55:28.463
And I love it because it
proves that exercise pays off.

01:55:28.463 --> 01:55:29.380
ANDY GALPIN: Oh, yeah.

01:55:29.380 --> 01:55:31.505
ANDREW HUBERMAN: It's one
of the few things in life

01:55:31.505 --> 01:55:33.850
where there's a direct
relationship between work

01:55:33.850 --> 01:55:34.540
and outcome.

01:55:34.540 --> 01:55:35.710
ANDY GALPIN: Yeah.

01:55:35.710 --> 01:55:38.560
As Henry Rollins described
in his wonderful essay,

01:55:38.560 --> 01:55:40.180
if you're familiar with that.

01:55:40.180 --> 01:55:41.778
Oh my gosh, you're
a punk rock guy.

01:55:41.778 --> 01:55:42.820
You know Henry, I'm sure.

01:55:42.820 --> 01:55:44.987
ANDREW HUBERMAN: I mean, I
certainly know who he is,

01:55:44.987 --> 01:55:46.300
and I know his work.

01:55:46.300 --> 01:55:47.050
ANDY GALPIN: Yeah.

01:55:47.050 --> 01:55:49.170
He has incredible
one-page paper.

01:55:49.170 --> 01:55:51.220
It's something to
do with the iron.

01:55:51.220 --> 01:55:53.110
And he basically
